&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wealth Management Speaker Series: How I Built(d) My Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In wealth management, organic growth can be hard to attain, but there are many ways of building a successful business. Come and hear from successful advisors from different business models and firm types about how they built and continue to grow their practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key questions to be explored include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Different career paths and journeys to success in wealth management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How to gain initial traction ... and continue growing over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lessons learned and practical tips&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Panelists include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alex Fedynsky, Partner at Aaron Wealth Advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Andrew Leonard, CEO at Geometric Wealth Advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Justin Padgett, President at Valeo Financial Advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This session will be moderated by Philipp Hecker, Chief Executive Officer at Bento Engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
The Wealth Management Speaker Series is brought to you by Columbia&amp;rsquo;s Wealth Management master&amp;rsquo;s program. Uniquely designed to educate working professionals, this 16-month, part-time online program prepares experienced and aspiring wealth management professionals to meet the disruptive challenges of today&amp;rsquo;s industry. The innovative and rigorous curriculum connects advanced theory with practical applications through problem-based learning while providing students with the educational requirements for CFP certification.&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
